IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgf-s216a`
IMPORT `sg-proc-derivative-action`

-- Tests for sg-proc-derivative-action.l4 (s 216A and s 216B: the procedure for a statutory derivative action).
-- Every expected outcome below was written from the text (src:21784-21884 of CoA1967.txt) before the module was run,
-- never copied from its output. A trace that does not match is a finding. Day 0 of each trace is the day the TIMELINE line above its rule names.

§ `s 216A(3)(a): the notice to the directors`

-- The complainant gives the notice: no time limit.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant may give the directors notice of the intention to apply to the Court` (Individual "C") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(3)(a) give the directors of the company notice of the intention to apply to the Court` AT 2

-- No notice yet: the permission stays open, nothing is breached.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(3)(a) the complainant may give the directors notice of the intention to apply to the Court` (Individual "C") AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 216A(2) to (4): the application and the Court's decision`

-- Arguments: the complainant; the person is a complainant; what the application is for; the number of directors; the number of directors given the notice;
-- the notice stated the intention to apply; the day the notice was given; the day the complainant applies; acting in good faith; prima facie in the interests of the company;
-- the complainant has established that it is not expedient to give notice. Notice on 1 March 2026 (day 0) allows an application from 15 March (day 14).

-- In time: the application on 20 March (day 19), well after the 14 days, and the Court grants on day 25.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 19
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 25

-- The earliest day: the application on 15 March (day 14) is 14 days after the notice, and the Court grants on day 20.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 14
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 20

-- One day short: the application on 14 March (day 13) gives only 13 days' notice; the Court cannot be satisfied, so the grant is not open to it and the refusal still is.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 13
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 20

-- One day short, and the Court refuses on day 20: the application is answered.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 13
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(3) the Court refuses permission` AT 20

-- All three conditions hold, and the Court still refuses: being satisfied is necessary, not sufficient.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 19
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(3) the Court refuses permission` AT 25

-- The complainant is not acting in good faith: the bar applies, the grant is not open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 19
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 25

-- It does not appear prima facie in the interests of the company: the bar applies.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 19
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 25

-- The company has two directors and only one was given the notice: the notice is not 14 days' notice to the directors; the bar applies.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 2 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 19
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 25

-- Subsection (4): no notice was given and it is not expedient; the Court makes an interim order on day 3 and the complainant gives the notice on day 10.
-- The order was made "pending the complainant giving notice as required" (src:21830-21831): the application for permission is still undecided, so the rule stays open.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: the notice ends the interim order's wait and not the application, which the Court has still to grant or refuse (src:21830-21831)
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 0
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(4) the Court makes an interim order pending the notice` AT 3
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(4) give the directors the notice that the interim order awaits` AT 10

-- Subsection (4), after the notice: the Court grants permission on day 30; the application is answered.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 0
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(4) the Court makes an interim order pending the notice` AT 3
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(4) give the directors the notice that the interim order awaits` AT 10
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 30

-- Subsection (4), after the notice: the Court refuses on day 30; the application is answered.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 0
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(4) the Court makes an interim order pending the notice` AT 3
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(4) give the directors the notice that the interim order awaits` AT 10
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(3) the Court refuses permission` AT 30

-- Subsection (4), the Court grants on day 23, the 13th day after the notice of day 10: the 14 days' notice (s 216A(3)(a), src:21811) have not run out, the Court cannot be satisfied, so the grant is not open and the rule stays open (the refusal still is).
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 0
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(4) the Court makes an interim order pending the notice` AT 3
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(4) give the directors the notice that the interim order awaits` AT 10
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 23

-- Subsection (4), the Court grants on day 24, the 14th day after the notice of day 10: the 14 days have run out, and the application is answered.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 0
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(4) the Court makes an interim order pending the notice` AT 3
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(4) give the directors the notice that the interim order awaits` AT 10
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 24

-- Subsection (4), the Court refuses on day 13, the 3rd day after the notice: the refusal is open at once, and the application is answered.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 0
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(4) the Court makes an interim order pending the notice` AT 3
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(4) give the directors the notice that the interim order awaits` AT 10
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(3) the Court refuses permission` AT 13

-- Subsection (4), after the notice, but the complainant is not acting in good faith: the grant is not open (s 216A(3)(b)), only the refusal is, so a grant on day 30 leaves the rule open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 0
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(4) the Court makes an interim order pending the notice` AT 3
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(4) give the directors the notice that the interim order awaits` AT 10
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(2) the Court grants permission` AT 30

-- Subsection (4), second step not taken: after the interim order the notice is still awaited; the text sets no time, so nothing is breached.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 0
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(4) the Court makes an interim order pending the notice` AT 3
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Subsection (4) not made out (the complainant has not established that notice is not expedient): the interim order is not open to the Court.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 0 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 0
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(4) the Court makes an interim order pending the notice` AT 3

-- The application is made and the Court has not decided: no time limit on the Court.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "C" DOES `s 216A(2) apply to the Court for permission to bring or intervene in the action or arbitration` AT 19
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- No application is made: the complainant may apply, and has no last day.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Gate fails: the person is not a complainant, so subsection (2) grants nothing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") FALSE `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Gate fails: the application is for some other purpose than the four the subsection names.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(2) the complainant may apply to the Court for permission and the Court decides` (Individual "C") TRUE `s 216A(2) for some other purpose` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 216A(5): the orders in granting permission`

-- Arguments: the order in question; the Court is granting permission; a person has been authorised to control the conduct; the fees are reasonable; the fees were incurred by the complainant.

-- (a), the Court is granting permission: it orders on day 3.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(5) the Court may make the order in granting permission` `s 216A(5)(a) the order about who controls the conduct of the action or arbitration` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(5)(a) the Court orders that the complainant or another person controls the conduct of the action or arbitration` AT 3

-- (a), no order yet: the power stays open and the text sets no day.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(5) the Court may make the order in granting permission` `s 216A(5)(a) the order about who controls the conduct of the action or arbitration` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- (a), gate fails: the Court is not granting permission; the subsection says nothing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(5) the Court may make the order in granting permission` `s 216A(5)(a) the order about who controls the conduct of the action or arbitration` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- (b), a person has been authorised: directions on day 2.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(5) the Court may make the order in granting permission` `s 216A(5)(b) the order giving directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(5)(b) the Court gives directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person so authorised` AT 2

-- (b), gate fails: no person has been authorised, so there is no "person so authorised" to direct.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(5) the Court may make the order in granting permission` `s 216A(5)(b) the order giving directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- (c), the fees are reasonable and incurred by the complainant: the order on day 2.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(5) the Court may make the order in granting permission` `s 216A(5)(c) the order about the complainant's legal fees and disbursements` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216A(5)(c) the Court orders the company to pay the complainant's reasonable legal fees and disbursements` AT 2

-- (c), still open: no order made.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216A(5) the Court may make the order in granting permission` `s 216A(5)(c) the order about the complainant's legal fees and disbursements` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- (c), gate fails: the fees are not reasonable.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216A(5) the Court may make the order in granting permission` `s 216A(5)(c) the order about the complainant's legal fees and disbursements` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 216B(1): no stay or dismissal by reason only of the members' approval`

-- Arguments: the application or action is under section 216A; the only reason for the stay or dismissal is the members' approval.

-- The Court stays the action by reason only of the members' approval: the text says it must not be, and names no one who is bound.
-- The stay is an order made on a ground the subsection excludes; the rule ends FULFILLED, a closed route and not a breach by the Court.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: the passive "must not be stayed or dismissed" names no bearer and states no consequence, so no BREACH by the Court (src:21862-21864)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216B(1) the Court must not stay or dismiss by reason only of the members' approval` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216B(1) the Court stays or dismisses the application or action by reason only of the members' approval` AT 4

-- The Court does not: the bar stands, with no end date, so it is still in force.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216B(1) the Court must not stay or dismiss by reason only of the members' approval` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Gate fails: approval by the members is not the only reason, so the bar does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216B(1) the Court must not stay or dismiss by reason only of the members' approval` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216B(1) the Court stays or dismisses the application or action by reason only of the members' approval` AT 4

-- Gate fails: the action is not one under section 216A.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216B(1) the Court must not stay or dismiss by reason only of the members' approval` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 216B(2): the Court's approval of a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal`

-- Arguments: under section 216A; the Court is giving its approval; the Court has determined that the interest of a complainant may be substantially affected.

-- The Court approves on day 2 and, the complainant's interest being affected, orders notice on day 5.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216B(2) the Court may approve the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal and order notice to the complainant` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216B(2) the Court approves the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal` AT 2
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216B(2) the Court orders a party to give notice to the complainant` AT 5

-- The Court approves and may still order notice: the power is open, with no day.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216B(2) the Court may approve the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal and order notice to the complainant` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216B(2) the Court approves the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal` AT 2
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- The complainant's interest is not affected: the approval alone ends the rule, and the notice order is not open.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216B(2) the Court may approve the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal and order notice to the complainant` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216B(2) the Court approves the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal` AT 2

-- No approval yet: the Court's power stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216B(2) the Court may approve the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal and order notice to the complainant` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Gate fails: the Court is not giving its approval.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216B(2) the Court may approve the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal and order notice to the complainant` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 216B(3): interim costs`

-- The Court orders interim costs "at any time": on day 90 it is still in order.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216B(3) the Court may at any time order the company to pay the complainant interim costs` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Court DOES `s 216B(3) the Court orders the company to pay the complainant interim costs` AT 90

-- No order yet: the power stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216B(3) the Court may at any time order the company to pay the complainant interim costs` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Gate fails: the proceedings are not under section 216A.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216B(3) the Court may at any time order the company to pay the complainant interim costs` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN: the stable build 112 matches 41 of 43 while the unstable build (20261126, 90eed8e; the first run was on 20261125, a50cbd0) matches all 43; 2 traces read differently there (the #TRACE line, the expectation written from the text, what MAIN prints):
--   line 88: expected FULFILLED, MAIN prints RESIDUAL: Subsection (4), after the notice: the Court grants permission on day 30; the application is answered.
--   line 112: expected FULFILLED, MAIN prints RESIDUAL: Subsection (4), the Court grants on day 24, the 14th day after the notice of day 10: the 14 days have run out, and the application is answered.
--   Why: after the notice the grant sits behind the wait act of 13 days, a MAY that runs out (the device of sg-proc-compulsory-acquisition.l4, s 215(6)); on main a grant made after that MAY has run out is not taken as done, and the trace ends with the Court's two MAYs still open, where unstable takes the LEST and the helper that follows it. Observed end states only: this file does not say why main reads these differently, and the module is not changed to suit it. The refusal after the wait reads the same on both.
--   Every other trace gives the same class (FULFILLED, BREACH or RESIDUAL) on the stable build as on the unstable one; the one difference of print is that a still-open MAY is laid out on one line by the unstable build and on three lines by the stable build.
